§ `Tests of the control, the substitution the amendment writes, and the sources`

-- The control points at what it says.
#ASSERT `the reference points at what the Law names today` (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), regulation 1`)
-- Fork F2. What the amendment itself writes in place of what the words name: the Institute for the committee (SH 2774 p.152, ss 2 to 4), section 225(a1) for section 232 in section 225B(a) only (s 4), nothing for the control.
-- These are green: they record what the amendment writes. Whether the regulations are read through that substitution is the fork, and is not asserted.
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 2(c)(1), the committee`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS JUST `the Institute, which the Law now names where it named the committee`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), the committee`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS JUST `the Institute, which the Law now names where it named the committee`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(b), the committee`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS JUST `the Institute, which the Law now names where it named the committee`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 4(a), the committee`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS JUST `the Institute, which the Law now names where it named the committee`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), section 232`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS JUST `section 225(a1) of the Law, which the amendment writes where section 225B(a) named section 232`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), regulation 1`)'s `the amendment writes in place of what the words name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where each limb was read from.
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 2(c)(1), the committee`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(b), the committee`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), the committee`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 4(a), the committee`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), regulation 1`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- The day the new regime begins: a claim submitted from 1 June 2019 (Sefer HaChukim 2774 p. 153, s 7; 27 Iyar 5779 = 1 June 2019 on the calendar routine).
#ASSERT `the target stands in the Law for a claim submitted on` (`reference: long-term care regs r 2(c)(1), the committee`) (Date 1 6 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the Law for a claim submitted on` (`reference: long-term care regs r 2(c)(1), the committee`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the Law for a claim submitted on` (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), section 232`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A claim submitted before 1 June 2019: NOTHING. The pages read show no saving for such a claim in ss 5 and 6 and no rule that the committee stays for it; the answer is not given either way (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the target stands in the Law for a claim submitted on` (`reference: long-term care regs r 2(c)(1), the committee`) (Date 31 5 2019) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The control has no recorded change: NOTHING, which is not a statement that regulation 1 stands.
#ASSERT `the target stands in the Law for a claim submitted on` (`reference: long-term care regs r 3(a), regulation 1`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
